      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "An 80-year-old man is described with a left-sided recurrent laryngeal nerve palsy after primary total hip arthroplasty. Intubation was uncomplicated. Aetiology is discussed. It might be caused by intubation injury, stretch-induced injury due to cervical hyperextension or inappropriate positioning during surgery in the lateral approach or a combination."},
